window.COPART_KB_DATA = [{"id":"auction-access-overview","section":"Auction access","question":"Auction access","kind":"overview","html":"<p>What is Auction Access      * An Auction Access account in the U.</p><p>S. and Canada is a mandatory digital credential for licensed auto dealers to access over 400 wholesale vehicle auctions</p><ul><li>It verifies dealer credentials, provides a central login, enables mobile bidding via QR code, and links to floor plan financing, streamlining the purchase of wholesale vehicles for resale</li><li>The membership has an annual cost and requires dealer licensing for eligibility</li></ul><p>Copart registration via Auction Access</p>"},{"id":"auction-access-can-an-authorized-representative-create-a-copart-account-using-au","section":"Auction access","question":"Can an authorized representative create a Copart account using Auction access credentials?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>No. Only owner or manager role is authorized to create a Copart account using Auction access. An authorized representative would need to contact Auction access to make changes on the acc</p>"},{"id":"auction-access-what-documents-need-to-be-submitted-to-copart-while-linking-an-ac","section":"Auction access","question":"What documents need to be submitted to Copart while linking an account using Auction access?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>The user needs to complete the applicable Copart eSign document to complete the registration. Multistate or State tax form. In a handful of states, the Sales tax license or W9 may be required</p>"},{"id":"auction-access-what-documents-are-not-required-while-creating-a-copart-account-u","section":"Auction access","question":"What documents are not required while creating a Copart account using Auction access?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Dealer licenses and Photo Ids are not uploaded directly to Copart. The documents are mapped from the Auction ACCESS account</p><p>If any of the above documents are not linked to the Auction Access account, they must be uploaded to the Auction access account</p>"},{"id":"auction-what-is-virtual-live-auction","section":"Auction","question":"What is Virtual Live Auction?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>A Virtual Live Auction is a real-time, internet-only auction. On the day of the sale, lots are arranged by item number and divided into separate lanes that run simultaneously</p><p>When a lot is “on the block,” members place bids online in real time, competing with other members and any bids from the Preliminary Bidding period. Copart’s automated system, BID4U, submits bids on behalf of members who placed preliminary bids, up to their maximum bid</p>"},{"id":"auction-how-can-we-join-an-auction","section":"Auction","question":"How can we join an Auction?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Active Membership Requirement-</p><p>All participants must have an active Copart Member account to access or join an auction</p><p>Member Types and Access-</p><p>Guest Member: Can view one auction at a time</p><p>Basic Member: Can view multiple auctions simultaneously</p><p>Premier Member: Can view multiple auctions simultaneously</p><p>Eligibility to Participate in Live Auctions-</p><p>To bid in a live auction, members must:</p><p>Hold a paid membership (Basic or Premier)</p><p>Be eligible to bid on the specific lot</p><p>Have sufficient buying power or available bids to place offers</p><p>Important Notes-</p><p>Guest members can only observe auctions and cannot place bids</p>"},{"id":"auction-what-are-the-different-types-of-auctions-and-their-timings","section":"Auction","question":"What are the different types of Auctions and their timings?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Today’s Auctions-</p><p>Displays all auctions scheduled for the current day</p><p>Can be sorted by sale time, location, or region</p><p>Live Auction Bidding-</p><p>Combines physical (in-person) and virtual (online) bidding into a single real-time event</p><p>Virtual bids are announced during live auctions</p><p>Copart may extend bidding time at its discretion</p><p>Saturday Auctions-</p><p>Conducted for specialty sales such as powersports, heavy equipment, or rental fleet liquidations</p><p>Some locations may schedule Saturday auctions based on demand</p><p>Members should check the Auction Calendar for availability</p><p>VIX (Virtual Information Exchange)-</p>"},{"id":"auction-what-time-do-the-auctions-run-and-how-can-we-find-the-information-based-","section":"Auction","question":"What time do the Auctions run and how can we find the information based on locations?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Most Auctions start at 12 pm local time, but locations in the Eastern time zone begin at 10am</p><p>Most locations will have auctions on the same day and time each week</p><p>To find information about all auction days and times, members can visit the “Copart Auction Calendar” under the “Auctions” tab on the Copart home page</p><p>Members can also find more information about auctions at specific Copart locations (Select “Locations” tab then select desired yard location)</p>"},{"id":"auction-what-are-item-numbers","section":"Auction","question":"What are Item Numbers?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Item numbers represent the order in which the lots will be sold during the live auction portion of VB3. Sales with a large number of items are broken down into lanes</p>"},{"id":"auction-what-are-lanes","section":"Auction","question":"What are Lanes?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>A Copart Lane is one of several auctions from a single yard, running at the same time simultaneously. Each lane (like Lane A, B, or C) sells a different group of vehicles, often organized by type, seller, or condition, so multiple auctions can happen in parallel at the same time. This lets buyers jump directly into the lane that matches what they’re looking for and speeds up the entire sale</p>"},{"id":"auction-can-members-view-multiple-auctions-at-a-time","section":"Auction","question":"Can members view multiple auctions at a time?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Guest members can view 1 auction at a time</p><p>Basic and Premier members can view multiple auctions at a time (as many as there are running)</p><p>Once in the Live Auction, to add further Auctions, member would select “+ Add Auction” option</p>"},{"id":"auction-how-does-a-member-ensure-they-are-not-placing-bids-against-themselves-du","section":"Auction","question":"How does a member ensure they are not placing bids against themselves during Live Auction?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Members can view the “Previous Bids” section of the Live Auction to view past 2 bidders. Members will want to keep an eye on previous bids to ensure they are not placing the bids against themselves (as our system will allow them to do so)</p><p>Members can also pay attention to the sound the system makes. It will make a different sound when they place a bid versus when someone else places a bid</p>"},{"id":"auction-how-does-a-member-know-if-they-have-won-the-lot","section":"Auction","question":"How does a member know if they have won the lot?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>If they are participating in a live auction, the system will tell them that they have won</p><p>Members will be notified by email, text message, or push notification in the Copart Member App, depending on the methods they selected in the Preference Center</p><p>Members can also go into their Payments Due tab at the top of the page and see a list of vehicles they have won</p><p>In addition, members can check Bid status page to view, under Lots Won</p>"},{"id":"auction-member-adv-they-were-alerted-that-they-won-but-they-do-not-see-the-lot-i","section":"Auction","question":"Member adv they were alerted that they won, but they do not see the lot invoice in their Payments Due page, what happened?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Check the Sale Type, if it was “On Approval” or “Minimum Bid” it may be pending on approval from seller</p><p>On Approval - Seller has reserved the right to approve the final high bid achieved during the virtual auction</p><p>· Seller has until 7:45 p.m. PST one business day after the sale to accept, reject, or counter the winning bid</p><p>· The high bidder is obligated to purchase the vehicle if released by the Seller within the approval period</p><p>· The seller can accept the winning bid even if the buyer does not accept their counter</p>"},{"id":"bidding-process-overview","section":"BIDDING PROCESS","question":"BIDDING PROCESS","kind":"overview","html":"<p>To provide an overview of the bidding options available to Copart members and how they can participate in auctions</p>"},{"id":"bidding-process-what-is-the-bidding-process","section":"BIDDING PROCESS","question":"What is the Bidding Process?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>The bidding process allows a member to select a vehicle and place a bid during an auction. The outcome of the bid depends on the auction result and may or may not lead to winning the vehicle</p><p>How to join the Bidding Process?      Register as a Basic or Premier Member</p><p>Submit a valid Photo ID and Business License (if applicable)</p><p>Search for vehicles of interest</p><p>Add vehicles to the Watchlist or find a Broker (if required)</p><p>Join the relevant auction</p><p>Place bids on selected vehicles</p><p>Important Notes:</p><p>Once a bid is placed, it cannot be cancelled, deleted, or retracted</p>"},{"id":"bidding-process-what-are-the-different-types-of-bids","section":"BIDDING PROCESS","question":"What are the different types of bids?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Preliminary Bidding (Pre-Bids)-</p><p>Members can place bids before, and the pre-bid will close hortly 2 minutes before the vehicle goes for a live auction</p><p>These bids are automatically represented during the live auction</p><p>Members enter their maximum bid amount during preliminary bidding</p><p>The system automatically places bids on their behalf during the auction, up to the set limit</p><p>Live Bidding-</p><p>Members can place real-time bids when the vehicle is on the auction block using web or mobile devices</p><p>Only active accounts are allowed to participate in live bidding</p><p>Monster Bid-</p>"},{"id":"bidding-process-what-are-the-different-types-of-sales","section":"BIDDING PROCESS","question":"What are the different types of Sales?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>The vehicle is automatically awarded to the highest bidder at the end of the auction</p><p>No minimum price or seller approval is required</p><p>On Approval-</p><p>The seller reserves the right to accept, reject, or counter the highest bid</p><p>The decision must be made within one business day after the sale</p><p>The highest bidder is obligated to purchase if the seller accepts the bid within this period</p><p>Minimum Bid / On Reserve-</p><p>The seller sets a minimum price for the vehicle</p><p>If the minimum is not met, the seller may accept or reject the bid within one business day</p><p>Buy It Now-</p>"},{"id":"bidding-process-what-happens-after-the-lot-is-awarded","section":"BIDDING PROCESS","question":"What happens after the lot is awarded?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Once a lot is awarded, the member must complete payment and vehicle pickup within the required timelines</p><p>1. For Payment-</p><p>Payment must be made within 3 business days, including the sale day</p><p>A $50 late fee is charged if payment is not completed on time</p><p>If the lot is not paid within 8 calendar days, it will be relisted</p><p>For Buy It Now and Kiosk bids, the same 3-business-day payment rule applies; otherwise, the lot will be relisted</p><p>A relist fee of 10% of the sale price or $600 (whichever is higher) will be charged</p><p>2. For Vehicle Pickup-</p><p>Members must arrange pickup promptly to avoid daily storage charges</p><p>Free storage period:</p>"},{"id":"bidding-process-what-is-bid4u","section":"BIDDING PROCESS","question":"What is BID4U?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>BID4U is Copart’s automated bidding system where members place a Max Bid amount, and our system will auto outbids other members that place bids on the same lot, up to the max bid amount they placed</p>"},{"id":"bidding-process-what-are-bidding-alerts","section":"BIDDING PROCESS","question":"What are Bidding Alerts?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Buyers can set up alerts online to receive emails when items they are interested in go to Auction if this preference is selected under “Preference Center”</p><p>Buyers will receive emails/texts when items that are on their watchlist are up for Auction</p><p>They will receive email/text updates when a lot is awarded or a seller counters on their offer</p><p>Buyers will not receive notification if the lot is not awarded to them</p><p>Buyers may view their bid status online by going to their Dashboard, My Bids widget or Bid Status &gt; My Bids</p>"},{"id":"bidding-process-what-are-bid-increments","section":"BIDDING PROCESS","question":"What are bid increments?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Bid increments are the predetermined amounts by which a bid must be raised depending on the vehicle value. These increments are based on the current high bid of the lot- as the price of the vehicle increases; the bid increment also increases</p>"},{"id":"bidding-process-what-is-the-tiebreaker-option","section":"BIDDING PROCESS","question":"What is the TieBreaker option?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>The TieBreaker toggle, if selected, will automatically add one bid increment (for the bidder who activated it first) if member and another bidder have placed the same Maximum bid on the same lot</p>"},{"id":"bidding-process-can-a-pre-bid-be-retracted","section":"BIDDING PROCESS","question":"Can a Pre-bid be retracted?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Bids are unable to be retracted once placed. However, there may be a “mistype bid” option under lot details page that will allow members to lower their bid</p><p>The Mistype bid tool will only appear when someone else has placed a bid on the same lot. We recommend that members add the lot to their watchlist, to keep an eye on other bid activity</p><p>When someone else places a bid, the member will have the option to ‘lower your max bid’ to the increment just above the current bid</p><p>Mistype bid tool cannot be used if the member submitted a Monster Bid</p>"},{"id":"bidding-process-6-how-to-handle-a-call-if-a-member-is-requesting-ip-search-per-l","section":"BIDDING PROCESS","question":"6- How to handle a call if a member is requesting IP Search per lot being awarded onto their account that they claim they did not bid on?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Review the type of bid member placed and educate the Member</p><p>If the Member continues to dispute the bids, please advise them that they can relist the lot and educate them on relist fee</p><p>If the buyer asks if we do IP Searches, please apologize and let them know that Copart does not perform IP Searches (do not direct the buyer to yard to request IP Search)</p><p>To remove all active users from your account, contact Member Services. Your account may be suspended for 24 hours and identity verification will be required. You should also update your email/password and mailing address on file.</p>"},{"id":"bidding-process-can-a-member-purchase-a-vehicle-before-or-after-the-auction","section":"BIDDING PROCESS","question":"Can a Member purchase a vehicle before or after the Auction?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Members can purchase a vehicle before an action by searching for “Buy It Now” vehicles, or vehicles with the “Make An Offer” option</p><p>If the lot was awarded to another member, its possible it will relist if the sale isn’t successfully completed</p>"},{"id":"bidding-process-what-if-a-member-is-awarded-a-lot-but-does-not-wish-to-complete-","section":"BIDDING PROCESS","question":"What if a Member is awarded a lot but does not wish to complete the sale?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Please educate the member on relisting – if the lot is not paid within the 8 calendar days including day of sale, it will auto relist. If they wish to relist sooner, they will inquire with yard location</p><p>The relist fee will be 10% of sale price or $600, whichever is highest</p>"},{"id":"bidding-process-for-on-approval-on-reserve-sales-can-a-member-reject-the-sellers","section":"BIDDING PROCESS","question":"For On Approval/On Reserve sales, can a member reject the Sellers Counter bid?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Members can stay at their current bid or counter the sellers offer but they cannot reject the sellers counter</p><p>If the buyer does not accept the seller counter, the seller can still accept the original bid within the timeframe (7:45pm PST the following business day)</p>"},{"id":"bid-eligibility-revised-overview","section":"Bid Eligibility (revised)","question":"Bid Eligibility (revised)","kind":"overview","html":"<p>What is Bid Eligibility?      Bid Eligibility refers to the set of requirements a member must meet to be allowed to place a bid on a specific vehicle in a Copart auction</p>"},{"id":"bid-eligibility-revised-how-does-bidding-eligibility-work","section":"Bid Eligibility (revised)","question":"How does bidding eligibility work?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Bid eligibility is determined based on state regulations and vehicle-specific requirements. Each state has different laws regarding the licenses, documents, and credentials required to purchase a vehicle at auction</p><p>Members must have the required licenses for the state where the vehicle is located</p><p>All necessary documents must be uploaded and approved by Copart before bidding</p><p>Eligibility is based on the state of the lot and the vehicle’s title code</p><p>The Copart system determines bid eligibility in real time based on the documents available in the member’s account</p>"},{"id":"bid-eligibility-revised-how-does-a-member-check-their-eligibility-to-bid-on-a-lo","section":"Bid Eligibility (revised)","question":"How does a member check their eligibility to bid on a lot?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Members can verify their eligibility to bid on a lot on the Lot Details page, which shows a real-time Eligibility Status based on their account</p><p>If eligible, the status reads: “Eligible to bid.”</p><p>If ineligible, the status reads: “Not Eligible to Bid. Check Why?” Selecting “Check Why” provides details</p><p>If ineligible due to account status, the message explains the restriction</p><p>If ineligible due to missing or insufficient licenses, the message lists the license types required to become eligible</p>"},{"id":"bid-eligibility-revised-how-does-no-license-required-category-help-the-members","section":"Bid Eligibility (revised)","question":"How does No License Required category help the members?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>The No License Required category allows all Basic and Premier Members to bid on vehicles without a business license, provided they have the minimum deposit and a valid government-issued photo ID. Members can easily find eligible vehicles by going to Inventory &gt; Vehicle Finder, selecting “No License Required” under Featured Items, and using additional filters to refine their search</p>"},{"id":"bid-eligibility-revised-what-is-state-licensing-overview-and-where-can-we-find-i","section":"Bid Eligibility (revised)","question":"What is State Licensing Overview and where can we find it?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>The State Licensing Overview is a reference guide used by Copart to determine member bid eligibility based on:</p><p>Member’s active license type</p><p>State where the vehicle is located</p><p>Vehicle’s title type</p><p>Steps to find State Licensing Overview (Click on hyperlink):</p><p>Navigate to Services and Support &gt; Licensing Help</p><p>Find the section “Second Requirement: Business licensing, if you have them”</p><p>The State Licensing Overview Chart is by no means a comprehensive or complete listing of eligibility rules. Copart website will determine bid eligibility in real time based upon the licenses and documents the Members have on file</p>"},{"id":"bid-eligibility-revised-what-is-a-broker","section":"Bid Eligibility (revised)","question":"What is a Broker?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Brokers are third-party buyers who help facilitate vehicle purchases that require Members to have business licenses they may not have</p><p>If a member is not eligible to bid due to licensing, they may use a Broker or Market Maker</p><p>These can be found through the Copart Website, by selecting “Services and Support” then selecting “Brokers”</p>"},{"id":"bid-eligibility-revised-how-do-i-verify-if-a-member-is-able-to-bid","section":"Bid Eligibility (revised)","question":"How do I verify if a member is able to bid?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Verify they are current on membership (and has deposit on file, if required)</p><p>Verify all required documents are on file</p><p>Verify member is eligible to bid on the lot (use \"Check Eligibility” tool under “License Bid Eligibility tab in Portal)</p><p>Confirm that member has not exceeded their bid limits</p><p>If a member is current on membership, passes for bid eligibility and has not exceeded their bid limits, please utilize the “Refresh Eligibility” button via License Bid Eligibility tab in portal, then advise member to log out and back in to refresh. If that does not resolve, please continue with all basic troubleshooting steps</p>"},{"id":"bid-eligibility-revised-what-is-a-bid-card-and-when-is-it-required","section":"Bid Eligibility (revised)","question":"What is a BID Card and when is it required?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>BID Card stands for “Buyer Identification Card.”</p><p>Certain states require that a buyer has a specific BID Card from that state in order to bid on certain lot types</p><ul><li>Alabama requires an Alabama BID Card to bid on Salvage lots in Alabama</li><li>Michigan requires a Michigan BID Card to bid on Salvage lots in Michigan</li><li>Wisconsin requires a Wisconsin BID Card to bid on lots located in Wisconsin</li><li>Nevada requires a Nevada BID Card for buyers in Nevada to bid on lots in Nevada</li><li>Utah requires a Utah Salvage BID license for buyer in Utah to bid on Salvage lots in Utah</li></ul>"},{"id":"bid-eligibility-revised-does-copart-issue-bid-cards","section":"Bid Eligibility (revised)","question":"Does Copart issue BID Cards?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>No. The member needs to contact the state they wish to bid in to register for a BID Card</p><p>In order to use a BID Card, a member must have active Dealer or Dismantler licensing on file</p><p>If the member cannot get a BID Card, they will need to go through a Broker in order to bid on certain lots in that state. These regulations are made by the state, not Copart</p>"},{"id":"bid-eligibility-revised-bid-eligibility-tool-in-portal-fails-per-seller-restrict","section":"Bid Eligibility (revised)","question":"Bid Eligibility tool in portal fails per “Seller Restriction”, what does this mean?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>You may see this restriction reason for Licensed buyers who to not hold a Dealer license, but instead a General Business license (auto or non-auto related)</p><p>The seller has opted to NOT sell to non-Dealers</p><p>Let member know its being sold specifically to Dealers only</p>"},{"id":"bid-eligibility-revised-what-are-purchase-limits","section":"Bid Eligibility (revised)","question":"What are “Purchase Limits”?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>There are 4 States that have a purchase limit on how many salvage title vehicles a consumer can be awarded</p><p>In the State of Texas, there is a limit for consumers purchasing in their home State. They are limited to 5 salvage titles in a Calendar year. The only way to exceed that is to have a Dealer license on file</p><p>The state of Utah, there is a limit for consumers purchasing in their home state. They are limited to 5 salvage titles in a Rolling year. The only way to exceed that is to have a Salvage Dealer license on file</p>"},{"id":"bid-eligibility-revised-what-licensing-is-required-to-allow-a-member-to-bid-on-b","section":"Bid Eligibility (revised)","question":"What Licensing is required to allow a member to bid on Boats in Texas?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>In order for a member to bid on a Boat in TX they must have a Boat related Dealer license</p><p>Examples include; Boat Dealer, Marine Dealer, Vessel Dealer</p><p>Public and International buyers cannot bid on Boats in TX because they will not have this license type</p>"},{"id":"bid-eligibility-revised-what-are-the-requirements-for-a-consumer-to-bid-on-salva","section":"Bid Eligibility (revised)","question":"What are the requirements for a consumer to bid on salvage lots in Colorado?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Only Salvage titles that have the following Title Document disclosure are open to the Public in CO:</p><p>Public bill of sale parts</p><p>Reconstructed Permit to sell</p><p>Permit to sell</p><p>Parts only with no title</p><p>CO- Public – Salvage Title</p><p>Salvage lots from Yard 118 Colorado Springs will not be applicable for consumers, regardless of Title Document disclosure</p>"},{"id":"bid-eligibility-revised-how-can-an-unlicensed-buyer-search-for-lots-they-will-ha","section":"Bid Eligibility (revised)","question":"How can an unlicensed buyer search for lots they will have access to bid on?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>They can review State Licensing Overview</p><p>They can utilize the “No License Required” category</p><p>They can check eligibility by utilizing the bid eligibility tool on lot page</p>"},{"id":"bid-eligibility-revised-where-can-a-member-view-licensing-requirements-specific-","section":"Bid Eligibility (revised)","question":"Where can a member view Licensing requirements specific to their location on the Copart website?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>For Domestic Buyers- By selecting “Services and Support” &gt; Licensing Help &gt; Under “Business Licensing Map of State and Provinces” they can select the dropdown to select State/Province</p><p>For International Buyers- Bottom of website under “Services” &gt; select “International Buyers” &gt; select dropdown box to select Country</p>"},{"id":"buyer-power-bid-and-award-limit-overview","section":"Buyer Power, Bid and Award Limit","question":"Buyer Power, Bid and Award Limit","kind":"overview","html":"<p>What are Bid Limits?      Bid Limits define the maximum number of bids a member can place, the total number of lots they can be awarded, and the total dollar amount they are authorized to bid at one time. These limits are based on the member’s Membership plan and Deposit.that a member adds</p>"},{"id":"buyer-power-bid-and-award-limit-what-is-buying-power","section":"Buyer Power, Bid and Award Limit","question":"What is Buying Power?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Buying Power is the total dollar amount a member is authorized to use for placing bids in an auction</p><p>Example:If a member has $10,000 in Buying Power, they could bid $5,000 on Lot A, $4,000 on Lot B, and $1,000 on Lot C. Once the total bids reach $10,000, the member has reached their Buying Power limit. If a bid is unsuccessful, the corresponding amount is restored to the member’s Buying Power</p><p>Membership-Specific Limits:</p><p>Basic Membership: With Basic membership, members can bid up to $2,000 without a deposit. To bid higher, a 10% deposit of the total planned bids is required (e.g., $2,000 deposit for $20,000 in bids)</p>"},{"id":"buyer-power-bid-and-award-limit-what-is-bid-limit","section":"Buyer Power, Bid and Award Limit","question":"What is Bid limit?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Bid Limit defines the maximum number of preliminary bids a member can place at one time</p><p>Member-Specific Limits:</p><p>Basic Members: Can place 1 preliminary bid at a time. With a deposit on file, they can place up to 5 bids simultaneously</p><p>Premier Members: Can place up to 10 preliminary bids at a time</p>"},{"id":"buyer-power-bid-and-award-limit-what-is-award-limit","section":"Buyer Power, Bid and Award Limit","question":"What is Award limit?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Award Limit refers to the maximum number of lots a member can win or have pending payment, including:</p><p>Lots won but awaiting payment</p><p>Lots won in live auctions or involved in counter bids (On Approval / Minimum Bid)</p><p>Member-Specific Limits:</p><p>Basic Members: Can be awarded 1 lot at a time. With a deposit on file, they can be awarded up to 5 lots simultaneously</p><p>Premier Members: Can be awarded up to 3 lots at a time. Accounts created before 04/05/2023 can be awarded up to 5 lots at a time</p><p>Bid And Award Process Flow:-</p><p>The member places a bid, up to their available Buying Power</p>"},{"id":"buyer-power-bid-and-award-limit-member-has-exceeded-their-bid-limits-what-now","section":"Buyer Power, Bid and Award Limit","question":"Member has exceeded their bid limits, what now?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>If member hits their limit on high bid or award, this will prevent them from bidding further (they will get an error when attempting to bid that they have \"exceeded their bid limits\")</p><p>Basic members</p><ul><li>educate member that they can add a deposit on file (10% of buying power they wish to have) to allow them to place up to 5 bids at a time versus the 1 at a time without deposit</li><li>educate on upgrading to Premier where they can place up to 10 bids at a time, be awarded up to 3 lots at a time, up to $100,000 buying power</li><li>if they have exceeded their Award Limit, educate them to pay open invoice in full</li></ul><p>Premier members</p>"},{"id":"buyer-power-bid-and-award-limit-how-does-a-member-increase-their-buying-power","section":"Buyer Power, Bid and Award Limit","question":"How does a member increase their buying power?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>For Basic members, they go to the Payments tab, then select Deposits. They select “add a deposit”, then they enter the amount they wish to bid up to (total buying power they wish to obtain). Then our system will calculate the 10% of that amount. Then they choose the payment method they want to use to provide those funds</p>"},{"id":"buyer-power-bid-and-award-limit-basic-members-bid-limits-are-not-matching-deposi","section":"Buyer Power, Bid and Award Limit","question":"Basic members bid limits are not matching deposit on file, can I adjust?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Yes, Please adjust the bid limits to match the deposit on file</p><p>Go to the “License Bid Eligibility” tab and under “Bid limits” select pencil to edit &gt; adjust High bid limit to 5, adjust the Award limit to 5, adjust Buying Power accordingly (will be 10x the amount of deposit on file.) Ensure “Time Duration” remains at “Annual”, then select “Save”. Once completed, select the “Refresh Eligibility” button. (Advise the member to log out and back in to refresh, if they are currently logged in)</p><p>Example member has $500 deposit on file, the buying power will be $5,000</p>"},{"id":"buyer-power-bid-and-award-limit-premier-members-bid-limits-are-not-correct-can-i","section":"Buyer Power, Bid and Award Limit","question":"Premier members' bid limits are not correct, can I adjust?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Yes, Go to the “License Bid Eligibility” tab and under “Bid limits” select pencil to edit &gt; then select “Reset bid limits” &gt; ensure “ Time Duration” is set at “Daily” &gt; for Award limit, if account was created 4/5/2023 or later, adjust to 3 (if account was created prior to 4/5/2023, leave Award Limit at 5)  &gt;  then select “Save”. Once completed, select the “Refresh Eligibility” button. (Advise the member to log out and back in to refresh, if they are currently logged in)</p>"},{"id":"buyer-power-bid-and-award-limit-does-the-default-2-000-buyer-power-roll-over-onc","section":"Buyer Power, Bid and Award Limit","question":"Does the default $2,000 buyer power roll over once a Basic member adds a deposit on file?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>No, The $2,000 default buying power only applies to Basic member without a deposit on file</p><p>Once deposit is added, the buying power will be 10 times the amount of deposit added on file</p><p>Example, Basic member adds $325 deposit on file, their buying power will be $3,250 in total</p>"},{"id":"buyer-power-bid-and-award-limit-can-we-adjust-bid-limits-on-an-enterprise-bidder","section":"Buyer Power, Bid and Award Limit","question":"Can we adjust bid limits on an Enterprise bidder accounts?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>No, Member Services will never adjust status, bid limits of perform password resets for bidders. Enterprise will have access to self-service options online to manage their bidder accounts</p>"},{"id":"buyer-power-bid-and-award-limit-how-long-does-a-pre-bid-reserve-from-a-member-s-","section":"Buyer Power, Bid and Award Limit","question":"How long does a pre-bid reserve from a member’s bid limits?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>For pre-bids, they reserve until the member has been outbid by another member or until the lot goes into Live Auction</p>"},{"id":"buyer-power-bid-and-award-limit-how-long-does-an-award-limit-reserve-from-a-memb","section":"Buyer Power, Bid and Award Limit","question":"How long does an award limit reserve from a member's bid limits?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>If the lot is awarded to members account, it will reserve until paid in full</p><p>If the lot is pending seller approval, it will be reserved until either rejected per seller or awarded and invoice paid in full</p>"},{"id":"buyer-power-bid-and-award-limit-where-can-a-member-view-their-buying-power","section":"Buyer Power, Bid and Award Limit","question":"Where can a member view their buying power?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Members can view their total buying power under Payments &gt; Deposits</p>"},{"id":"cardholders-what-is-a-cardholder","section":"Cardholders","question":"What is a Cardholder?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>A Cardholder is an Authorized User (minimum 18 years of age) added to a Premier account by the Account Owner or Account Manager to act on their behalf for account-related activities</p><p>Privileges and Permissions Of A Cardholder -</p><p>Cardholders are granted the following rights:</p><p>Account Access: Authorized to contact Member Services and request specific account information</p><p>Yard Access: Permitted to visit any Copart yard location</p><p>Authorized Actions: Can perform formal account-related actions on behalf of the Account Owner, including making credit and debit card payments</p><p>Account Requirements-</p>"},{"id":"cardholders-how-is-the-cardholder-request-submitted","section":"Cardholders","question":"How is the Cardholder request submitted?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>The Owner can submit the form and the ID of the Cardholder by uploading  to their account via the Document Uploader</p>"},{"id":"cardholders-how-can-someone-delete-a-cardholder","section":"Cardholders","question":"How can someone Delete a Cardholder?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>The Owner must complete the Delete Cardholder portion of the form and submit it to their account for processing via the Document Uploader</p>"},{"id":"cardholders-does-the-cardholder-have-their-own-credentials-to-login-to-the-accou","section":"Cardholders","question":"Does the Cardholder have their own credentials to login to the account online?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>No. Cardholders do not receive a Member number or Password to gain online account access. This information would be up to the Owner to share with the Cardholder</p>"},{"id":"condition-report-overview","section":"Condition Report","question":"Condition Report","kind":"overview","html":"<p>What is Condition Report? A Condition Report is a paid, on-demand vehicle inspection report prepared by Copart yard personnel that provides detailed and verified information on a vehicle’s condition. It includes visual assessments, equipment verification, tire details, and recorded media such as engine, interior, and exterior videos, enabling members to make informed bidding decisions with greater transparency than a standard listing</p><p>Ordering and Payment (Member Action)-</p><p>The member navigates to the Lot Details page on the Copart website</p><p>Selects “Condition Report” under Reports and Services</p>"},{"id":"deposit-process-overview","section":"Deposit process","question":"Deposit process","kind":"overview","html":"<p>The objective is to understand how deposits, empowers the member to increase their buying power/bid limits/award limits over and above the entitlement they have in a membership</p><p>Key Terms -</p><p>Deposit: A security amount that allows members to increase their buying power/bid limits/award limits beyond what their membership offers</p><p>Buying Power: The total amount a member can bid or have in active bids at one time</p><p>Bid Limits: The total number of lots that a member can place bids on</p><p>Award Limits: The total number of lots that a member can be awarded after bids are placed</p><p>Basic Members -</p>"},{"id":"deposit-process-how-to-add-deposits","section":"Deposit process","question":"How to add Deposits ?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Advise member to log in to Copart website/app</p><p>Guide member to find Payment option below search bar on the website and three horizontal lines at the left side of the screen on the app</p><p>Under payments, ask member to select deposit</p><p>Explain member to mention the desired buying power they would like to add and confirm the same with the member (Example - $500 for $5000 buying power)</p>"},{"id":"deposit-process-2-what-is-buying-power","section":"Deposit process","question":"2. What is Buying Power?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Buying Power is the total amount you can bid at one time, including all active bids. If you lose a bid, that amount is automatically returned to your Buying Power</p>"},{"id":"deposit-process-3-how-much-can-i-bid-as-a-basic-member-without-a-deposit","section":"Deposit process","question":"3. How much can I bid as a Basic Member without a deposit?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Basic Members can bid up to $2,000 without making a deposit.4. How is Buying Power calculated for Basic Members?</p><p>Basic Members need to deposit 10% of their intended Buying Power.</p><p>Example:</p><p>$20,000 Buying Power → $2,000 deposit</p>"},{"id":"deposit-process-5-can-i-place-multiple-bids-at-the-same-time","section":"Deposit process","question":"5. Can I place multiple bids at the same time?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Yes, as long as the total of all active bids does not exceed your Buying Power</p><p>6. Can a Premier Member refund the $400 deposit and stay Premier?</p><p>No. Refunding the deposit downgrades the account to Basic</p><p>7. Can a Premier Member bid over $100,000 without adding a deposit?</p><p>Yes, with prior approval based on account history</p><p>8. Are wallet payments refundable after 90 days?</p><p>No. Wallet payments must be refunded within 90 calendar days</p><p>9. Can an account remain active during a Premier refund?</p><p>Yes, if downgraded to Basic</p>"},{"id":"deposit-process-10-how-does-deposit-help-us-prevent-fraud","section":"Deposit process","question":"10. How does deposit help us prevent fraud?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>If a member fails to make payment towards the purchased lots, our system uses the deposit on file towards the clearance of unpaid relist and the remaining will be asked to pay along with other open invoices if any on member’s account</p>"},{"id":"duplicate-title-overview","section":"Duplicate Title","question":"Duplicate Title","kind":"overview","html":"<p>What is Duplicate title?</p><p>A duplicate title is an official replacement copy of a vehicle’s original ownership document, issued by the relevant DMV when the original title is lost, damaged, or misplaced</p><p>Process to Request Duplicate Title -</p><p>Initiation: Member navigates to Payments &gt; History &gt; Invoice View and selects \"Order Replacement Title\"</p><p>Verification: Member enters the Lot # or VIN. The system verifies ownership and eligibility</p><p>Shipping Setup: Member confirms the mailing address and selects a shipping method</p>"},{"id":"fee-type-vehicle-cost-estimate-sop-overview","section":"Fee Type Vehicle Cost Estimate - SOP","question":"Fee Type Vehicle Cost Estimate - SOP","kind":"overview","html":"<p>Fee Structure:All vehicle purchases have the following fees: Sale Price +Buyer fee – based on title type and sale price of the vehicle. +Internet bid fee - based on title type and sale price of the vehicle. +Gate fee - $79 for clean title and $95 for non-clean title type vehicles. +Environmental fee - $0 for clean title and $15 for non-clean title type vehicles. There may also be a charge for sales tax depending on the state the vehicle is located in.</p>"},{"id":"fee-type-vehicle-cost-estimate-sop-do-we-have-a-fixed-buyer-fee-or-a-defined-per","section":"Fee Type Vehicle Cost Estimate - SOP","question":"Do we have a fixed buyer fee or a defined percentage for buyer fees?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>No. Buyer fees are not based on a fixed percentage. They vary depending on the sale price, title type, and membership type</p>"},{"id":"fee-type-vehicle-cost-estimate-sop-where-on-the-website-can-members-see-the-diff","section":"Fee Type Vehicle Cost Estimate - SOP","question":"Where on the website can members see the different fees and how they are calculated?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>The schedule of fees can be found on our website by clicking on your Profile Icon in the right corner of your account&gt;Member Fees</p>"},{"id":"fee-type-vehicle-cost-estimate-sop-is-the-gate-fee-refundable-if-i-load-the-car-","section":"Fee Type Vehicle Cost Estimate - SOP","question":"Is the Gate Fee refundable if I load the car myself?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>No. The Gate Fee covers administrative costs and the movement of the vehicle by Copart staff from the storage row to the loading area. It is mandatory for all purchases</p><p>Member payments &gt; Open Invoices &gt; Select the lot &gt; You can see sfd option. Once you click on that you can see the actual total and the discounted total if paid with secured funds</p>"},{"id":"membership-type-fees-overview","section":"Membership Type & Fees","question":"Membership Type & Fees","kind":"overview","html":"<p>Copart memberships give you access to live auctions and bidding, with options tailored for both occasional and frequent buyers. Membership fees support secure auctions and platform services and are separate from vehicle purchase costs and refundable deposits</p><p>1. Registration</p><p>User registers on the Copart website with basic details and email</p><p>System emails login credentials</p><p>2. Membership Selection</p><p>User selects a membership:</p><p>Guest (Free)</p><p>Basic ($99)</p><p>Premier ($249)</p><p>Applicable fees are paid during registration</p><p>3. Guest Membership (Free)</p><p>Account activated with view-only access</p>"},{"id":"membership-type-fees-what-document-is-auto-approved-by-veriff","section":"Membership Type & Fees","question":"What document is auto-approved by Veriff?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>When does Veriff approve a PID partially?</p><p>Below are the possible reasons for partial approval</p><p>Name mismatch</p><p>Duplicate account</p><p>Screen shot upload</p><p>Data missing or unclear</p><p>Different country PID</p><p>Three resubmissions</p><p>Document type not supported</p><p>Expired document</p>"},{"id":"membership-type-fees-what-are-the-different-types-of-titles","section":"Membership Type & Fees","question":"What are the different types of titles?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Clean Title – It indicates that the vehicle has no history of being \"totaled\" by an insurance company</p><p>Salvage Title - It is issued when a vehicle has been damaged to the extent that the cost of repair is deemed uneconomical by an insurance provider, or the vehicle has been stolen and recovered after a settlement was reached</p>"},{"id":"membership-type-fees-what-are-the-wallet-questions-based-on","section":"Membership Type & Fees","question":"What are the wallet questions based on?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Copart uses EVS (an electronic verification system) tailored to meet our unique fraud risk and compliance requirements</p><p>The wallet questions are an output of this tool</p>"},{"id":"membership-type-fees-what-are-the-examples-of-wallet-questions","section":"Membership Type & Fees","question":"What are the examples of Wallet questions?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Questions range from previous addresses, street names, zip codes, counties, and area codes associated with the user within 'x' amount of years. Or maybe people that are associated with them</p>"},{"id":"membership-type-fees-what-are-the-different-types-of-business-licenses","section":"Membership Type & Fees","question":"What are the different types of business licenses?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Dealer | Dismantler | Exporter | General business</p>"},{"id":"membership-fee-refund-sop-if-a-premier-member-requests-only-a-deposit-refund-can","section":"Membership fee Refund SOP","question":"If a Premier member requests only a deposit refund, can the agent downgrade the account to Basic and email the refunds team?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Account Information &gt; Membership Details: Under Membership history you will find “refund payment” option</p>"},{"id":"membership-fee-refund-sop-a-member-canceled-their-account-received-an-online-ref","section":"Membership fee Refund SOP","question":"A member canceled their account, received an online refund, and then purchased a membership again the next day. Can another refund be processed?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>No. The member should be informed about the earlier online refund and advised that this is considered a renewal refund as per policy</p>"},{"id":"membership-fee-renewal-refund-overview","section":"Membership fee renewal refund","question":"Membership fee renewal refund","kind":"overview","html":"<p>The purpose of the Membership Fee Renewal process is to provide a guideline on the handling of renewal fee refund requests from members before and after the renewal of the account</p><p>Refund request before auto-renewal      If the member requests cancellation of auto-renewal, the first step is to attempt to retain the customer. If the customer insists, Contact follow self-serve steps. Self-Serve Steps : Login to your account.</p><p>Click on Profile Icon on top right &gt;&gt; click \"Account setting\".</p><p>Click on \"Membership\" Option on the next page.</p>"},{"id":"membership-fee-renewal-refund-when-does-copart-send-an-auto-renewal-reminder-to-","section":"Membership fee renewal refund","question":"When does Copart send an auto-renewal reminder to the member?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>It is triggered via email on the 30th day &amp; 1 day before renewal</p><p>Under Notes tab &gt; Filter: All Notes &gt; Enter “Auto Pay” in the search tab</p>"},{"id":"membership-fee-renewal-refund-can-we-deactivate-the-membership-auto-renewal-feat","section":"Membership fee renewal refund","question":"Can we deactivate the Membership auto-renewal feature on behalf of the member?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Self-help options are available, but deactivate it cannot be done on your behalf</p>"},{"id":"payment-mode-and-limitations-overview","section":"Payment Mode and Limitations","question":"Payment Mode and Limitations","kind":"overview","html":"<p>Payment Options Overview :-</p><p>Copart provides multiple payment methods for Members to pay for vehicles, fees, and related services. Payment options vary based on buyer type and geographic location. Members are encouraged to use electronic payment methods, as in-person payments at Copart facilities incur a surcharge of $20 per vehicle</p><p>Timely payment and vehicle pickup are required to avoid late payment and storage fees. Storage charges may vary by location</p><p>Payment Methods Classification: -Payment options are categorized into Non-Secure and Secure payment methods:</p><p>1. Non-Secure Payment Methods-</p>"},{"id":"payment-mode-and-limitations-how-is-it-different-from-epay","section":"Payment Mode and Limitations","question":"How is it different from ePay?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Company Checks: Physical payment method submitted at the yard</p><p>ePay: Electronic debit from the same registered bank account</p><p>Limitations:</p><p>Requires application approval (bank verification form)</p><p>Limit is determined based on:</p><p>Member’s average bank balance</p><p>Member’s purchase and payment history</p><p>6- Plaid-Definition: A secure platform that connects bank accounts for electronic payments via the Member portal</p>"},{"id":"payment-mode-and-limitations-how-is-it-different-from-epay","section":"Payment Mode and Limitations","question":"How is it different from ePay?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Plaid: Available for domestic consumer and business buyers</p><p>ePay: Available only for domestic business members</p><p>Limitations:</p><p>Available only to U.</p><p>S. buyers on Copart.com</p><p>Not available in Canada or Crashed Toys</p><p>International buyers may use Plaid if they have a U.</p><p>S.-based bank account</p><p>Purchase limits are based on:</p><p>Membership type</p><p>Account tenure</p><p>Purchase history</p><p>7- MoneyGram-Definition: A global peer-to-peer money transfer and payment service company, allowing users to send funds to over 200 countries and territories</p><p>8- Western Union-</p>"},{"id":"payment-mode-and-limitations-1-how-can-a-member-increase-their-credit-debit-card","section":"Payment Mode and Limitations","question":"1- How can a member increase their Credit/Debit card, or Mobile Wallet app purchase limits?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Card &amp; Mobile Wallet app payment limits are adjusted based on membership activity and cannot be increased by the Accounting Department.​</p>"},{"id":"payment-mode-and-limitations-2-how-can-a-member-increase-their-company-check-epa","section":"Payment Mode and Limitations","question":"2-How can a member increase their Company check / ePay purchase limits?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>3-Are there any fees associated with making a payment?</p><p>There is a $20 Onsite Payment fee when making a payment at a Copart facility. We strongly encourage members to use electronic payment methods</p>"},{"id":"payment-mode-and-limitations-4-where-can-i-find-a-member-s-limits","section":"Payment Mode and Limitations","question":"4-Where can I find a member’s limits?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>5-Do all yards accept cash?</p><p>Varies per yard, we strongly recommend contacting the yard before going to be sure they accept cash</p>"},{"id":"payment-mode-and-limitations-6-do-sublots-take-payments","section":"Payment Mode and Limitations","question":"6-Do Sublots take payments?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>No, the member/transporter will need to go to the main yard location to pay first, then go to the sublot for their vehicle</p>"},{"id":"payment-policy-overview","section":"Payment Policy","question":"Payment Policy","kind":"overview","html":"<p>Payment Policy &gt;</p>"},{"id":"payment-policy-what-is-the-main-policy-for-most-payment-methods","section":"Payment Policy","question":"What is the main policy for most payment methods?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>All payments made on the account must match the Owner name on the account. In addition to this, the billing address on card used for payment should match the physical address on member’s Copart account</p><p>An exception to this rule is the Initial Membership payment made by the Member using someone else’s card</p><p>Credit &amp; Debit Cards – Can be in the owner’s name or Cardholders’ name</p><p>Cash – Can be paid by a transporter for fees in the yard if needed</p>"},{"id":"payment-policy-what-are-the-different-invoices-that-a-member-can-make-a-payment-","section":"Payment Policy","question":"What are the different invoices that a member can make a payment to?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Standard lot invoice</p><p>Membership invoices</p><p>Membership Renewal invoices</p><p>Deposit invoices</p><p>Relist invoice</p><p>Vehicle Condition Reports invoices</p><p>Misc invoices - [Example: Vest fee from the yard]</p><p>Returned Payment / NSF invoice</p><p>Making a payment at the yard:</p><p>The member must log into the Copart app and utilize the Visitors Sign in option when they get there. They can indicate they are there to make a payment</p><p>Bring a Photo ID that matches the name on the card.​</p><p>Credit &amp; Debit Cards - The card must match the name of the account holder.​</p><p>In person, payments may be subject to lengthy waiting times</p>"},{"id":"payment-policy-how-can-a-member-add-funds-to-their-unapplied-funds","section":"Payment Policy","question":"How can a member add funds to their unapplied funds?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>A member can only add funds to their unapplied funds using wire transfer</p>"},{"id":"payment-policy-how-do-i-add-my-card-wallet-app-to-my-account","section":"Payment Policy","question":"How do I add my card/wallet app to my account?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Account Settings &gt; Payments &amp; Fees &gt; Manage Payments &gt; Add New Payment</p>"},{"id":"payment-policy-can-i-unapply-a-partial-payment-made","section":"Payment Policy","question":"Can I unapply a partial payment made?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Can a member use their deposit to pay for a lot?</p><p>No, deposits cannot be used toward awarded lots</p>"},{"id":"payment-policy-how-do-i-generate-a-wire-transfer-reference-number","section":"Payment Policy","question":"How do I generate a wire transfer reference number?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>https://www.copart.com/member-payments/unpaid-invoices &gt; Select the invoice(s) &gt; Pay Invoice &gt; Select wire transfer for the payment method &gt; Click on continue to next step &gt; Click on generate reference number &gt; Will take the member to the confirmation page which includes the reference number</p>"},{"id":"payment-policy-how-do-i-apply-for-epay-online","section":"Payment Policy","question":"How do I apply for epay online?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>They can apply by selecting the pop-up notification on their dashboard OR go to Account information &gt; Payments &amp; Fees &gt; Manage Payments to be taken through the online verification process</p>"},{"id":"payment-policy-when-is-a-voided-check-needed-when-applying-for-company-checks-or","section":"Payment Policy","question":"When is a voided check needed when applying for Company Checks or ePay?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>When the member sees “Needs Verification,” they need to send in a copy of a VOIDED Company Check to epaycompanycheck@copart.com</p>"},{"id":"payment-policy-where-do-i-add-plaid","section":"Payment Policy","question":"Where do I add plaid?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Members can go to Account Settings &gt; Payments and Fees &gt; Manage Payments &gt; Add Account button to add Plaid. They can also go under Add New Payment option within Manage Payments</p><p>They will be redirected to Plaid to set up their bank account and enter their phone number if they are an existing Plaid user</p><p>During the set-up process, use “Continue as guest” if they want to connect their Copart account and don’t have an existing Plaid account</p><p>They’ll be asked to select their bank institution</p>"},{"id":"payment-policy-how-does-plaid-work","section":"Payment Policy","question":"How does Plaid work?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Buyers with five or fewer previous vehicle purchases will need to wait for their bank account payment to be reconciled. The option to transport the vehicle or process the title will be disabled until these funds have cleared, which may take up to 2 business days from the date the payment is initiated.​</p><p>A message to these buyers advising of the reconciliation process will be visible on the payments page of the website, and the same alert will appear in the payments tab of their member accounts in MSM.​</p>"},{"id":"payment-policy-if-the-member-pays-using-moneygram-at-a-moneygram-location-what-d","section":"Payment Policy","question":"If the member pays using MoneyGram at a MoneyGram location, what do they need?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>If paying in person, the member will need to bring their photo id, account number, and Copart receive code (17170). Their account number is made up of their member number and at least one lot number</p><p>If the member only has a 5-digit member number, they will want to add a 0 at the beginning</p><p>Example: member 45722 will be 045722</p>"},{"id":"payment-rejections-overview","section":"Payment Rejections","question":"Payment Rejections","kind":"overview","html":"<p>Credit/Debit Card &amp; Mobile Wallet App Payment Failure Reasons:</p><ul><li><strong>The order has been rejected by Decision Manager using Debit Card</strong>: Decision manager is the rules Copart sets in Cyber source which is our online DD and CC platform. Rules could be AVS match, negative list, fraud score, etc</li><li><strong>General Decline of the card. No other information provided by the issuing bank</strong>: The payment was rejected by the issuing bank without providing a specific reason to Copart</li></ul><p>Funding Instrument in the PayPal account was declined by the processor or bank, or it can’t be used for this payment using PayPal</p>"},{"id":"preliminary-bidding-what-is-preliminary-bidding-and-how-does-it-work","section":"Preliminary Bidding","question":"What is Preliminary Bidding And How does it work?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Preliminary bidding, also called pre-bidding, allows members to place bids on vehicles before the live auction starts and while the auction is ongoing (before the vehicle’s turn comes up)</p><p>Members can enter their bids in advance from the lot details page by choosing the next bid amount (incremental value). These bids are then automatically carried into the live auction</p><p>If no one places a higher bid during the live auction, the pre-bid can become the winning bid. However, if there is a tie between a pre-bid and a live bid, the live (virtual) bidder will be considered the highest bidder</p>"},{"id":"preliminary-bidding-who-can-place-a-preliminary-bid","section":"Preliminary Bidding","question":"Who can place a Preliminary Bid?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>All Basic and Premier members can place preliminary (pre-) bids. To do this, the member’s account must be active and all required licenses must be on file</p><p>The members must also have enough available bid and buying power within their bid limits. If they have already reached or exceeded their bid limit, they will not be able to place a pre-bid</p>"},{"id":"preliminary-bidding-when-can-a-preliminary-bid-be-placed","section":"Preliminary Bidding","question":"When can a Preliminary Bid be placed?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Members can place a preliminary bid up to one hour before the live auction begins</p><p>Once the live auction has started, members can still place pre-bids until the vehicle is close to being auctioned, specifically, up to when the lot is about 2 units or 2 minutes away from going on the block (its turn in the live auction)</p><p>Bid Types for Preliminary Bid</p><p>Incremental Bid: An Incremental Bid is a one-time increase. A member can simply place a bid at the next required increment above the current high bid</p>"},{"id":"preliminary-bidding-once-a-pre-bid-is-placed-where-can-a-member-view-the-bid-on-","section":"Preliminary Bidding","question":"Once a Pre-bid is placed, where can a member view the bid on their account?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>They can view current bids from their Dashboard under the “Bids” section, and from their “my bids” page (Bid status &gt; My bids)</p>"},{"id":"preliminary-bidding-can-a-pre-bid-be-retracted","section":"Preliminary Bidding","question":"Can a Pre-bid be retracted?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Bids are unable to be retracted once placed. However, there may be a “mistype bid” option under lot details page that will allow members to lower their bid. This option is not a default tab available for all the lots but would vary at a lot level</p><p>How does “mistype bid” tool work?</p><p>The Mistype bid tool will only appear when someone else has placed a bid on the same lot. We recommend that members add the lot to their watchlist, to keep an eye on other bid activity</p><p>When someone else places a bid, the member will have the option to ‘lower</p><p>your max bid’ to the increment just above the current bid</p>"},{"id":"preliminary-bidding-what-are-bid-increments","section":"Preliminary Bidding","question":"What are bid increments?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Bid increments are the predetermined amounts by which a bid must be raised depending on the vehicle value. These increments are based on the current high bid of the lot- as the price of the vehicle increases; the bid increment also increases</p>"},{"id":"preliminary-bidding-if-a-lot-is-awarded-via-buy-it-now-or-kiosk-bid-feature-what","section":"Preliminary Bidding","question":"If a lot is awarded via Buy It Now or Kiosk Bid feature, what virtual bid fee will apply?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Buy It Now and Kiosk Bids will be charged as a “pre-bid” for the virtual bid fee</p>"},{"id":"preliminary-bidding-what-is-the-tiebreaker-function","section":"Preliminary Bidding","question":"What is the TieBreaker function?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Lots will have a TieBreaker toggle option. When enabled, if member and another bidder have the same maximum bid placed, the tiebreak will automatically add one bid increment for the bidder who activated the tiebreaker first</p>"},{"id":"registration-process-overview","section":"Registration process","question":"Registration process","kind":"overview","html":"<p>The purpose of the Registration process is to list the flow for Individual &amp; Business account registration and a guideline on handling the member queries</p><p>Individual account registration      *  A member uses Copart website or the app to register</p><ul><li>Upon selecting the individual account, the member needs to enter individual name and email address, this leads to a creation of guest account</li><li>The member can sign up for either a basic or premier membership by paying $99 or $249 (membership fee) + $400 (one time deposit) respectively</li></ul><p>Payment Options</p>"},{"id":"registration-process-what-document-is-auto-approved-by-veriff","section":"Registration process","question":"What document is auto-approved by Veriff?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>When does Veriff approve a PID partially?</p><p>Below are the possible reasons for partial approval</p><p>Name mismatch</p><p>Duplicate account</p><p>Screen shot upload</p><p>Data missing or unclear</p><p>Different country PID</p><p>Three resubmissions</p><p>Document type not supported</p><p>Expired document</p>"},{"id":"registration-process-what-are-the-different-types-of-titles","section":"Registration process","question":"What are the different types of titles?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Clean Title – It indicates that the vehicle has no history of being \"totaled\" by an insurance company</p><p>Salvage Title - It is issued when a vehicle has been damaged to the extent that the cost of repair is deemed uneconomical by an insurance provider, or the vehicle has been stolen and recovered after a settlement was reached</p>"},{"id":"registration-process-what-are-the-wallet-questions-based-on","section":"Registration process","question":"What are the wallet questions based on?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Copart uses EVS (an electronic verification system) tailored to meet our unique fraud risk and compliance requirements</p><p>The wallet questions are an output of this tool</p>"},{"id":"registration-process-what-are-the-examples-of-wallet-questions","section":"Registration process","question":"What are the examples of Wallet questions?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Questions range from previous addresses, street names, zip codes, counties, and area codes associated with the user within 'x' amount of years. Or maybe people that are associated with them</p>"},{"id":"registration-process-what-are-the-different-types-of-business-licenses","section":"Registration process","question":"What are the different types of business licenses?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Dealer | Dismantler | Exporter | General business</p>"},{"id":"sales-tax-credit-overview","section":"Sales Tax & Credit","question":"Sales Tax & Credit","kind":"overview","html":"<p>What is a Sales Tax Credit?</p><p>A Sales Tax Credit is:</p><p>A refund or adjustment of sales tax previously paid on a vehicle purchase</p><p>Applicable only when qualifying documentation is provided</p><p>Subject to approval based on complete and accurate supporting documents</p><p>General Sales Tax Rules For Different Accounts:-</p><ul><li>Dealer Accounts*</li></ul><p>Dealers are not charged sales tax if licensing is active at the time of purchase</p><p>If sales tax is charged:</p><p>Licensing was inactive at time of purchase, OR</p><p>Invoice remained open and licensing became inactive later</p><p>Action Required:</p><p>Buyer must update licensing</p>"},{"id":"sales-tax-credit-was-sales-tax-charged","section":"Sales Tax & Credit","question":"Was Sales Tax Charged?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Determine Eligibility for Tax Credit</p><p>Advise buyer of required documentation. Email necessary forms to buyer</p><p>Request that the buyer forwarded all required documentation to the Sales Tax Team</p>"},{"id":"schedule-pick-up-overview","section":"Schedule Pick Up","question":"Schedule Pick Up","kind":"overview","html":"<p>Scheduling a Vehicle Pickup (Self-Pickup)</p><p>1. Access: The member navigates to https://www.copart.com/member-payments/unpaid-invoices on Copart.com or the App</p><p>2. Selection: Expand the specific invoice or checkmark multiple invoices and select \"Schedule Pickup\" at the top of the screen</p><p>3. Method: Select the \"Pick it up myself\" option</p><p>4. Appointment Selection: Choose an available date and time slot based on yard capacity. Click \"Confirm Time.\"</p><p>5. Vehicle Details: Enter the details of the transport vehicle being used for the pickup and click \"Confirm Appointment.\"</p><p>6. Confirmation:</p>"},{"id":"schedule-pick-up-q-do-i-still-need-a-gate-pass-pin","section":"Schedule Pick Up","question":"Q: Do I still need a Gate Pass PIN?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>A: No. Scheduled pickups eliminate the need for a PIN</p>"},{"id":"schedule-pick-up-q-can-i-schedule-on-copart-ca","section":"Schedule Pick Up","question":"Q: Can I schedule on Copart.ca?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>A: No. Log in via Copart.com or the Mobile App</p>"},{"id":"schedule-pick-up-q-how-do-i-check-in","section":"Schedule Pick Up","question":"Q: How do I check in?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>A: Use the link sent via text. You must be within 1 mile of the yard and no later than 15 minutes past your time slot</p>"},{"id":"schedule-pick-up-q-what-if-i-m-late","section":"Schedule Pick Up","question":"Q: What if I’m late?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>A: After 15 minutes, the system cancels the appointment. You must reschedule via the app or website</p>"},{"id":"schedule-pick-up-q-why-am-i-seeing-an-out-of-range-error","section":"Schedule Pick Up","question":"Q: Why am I seeing an \"Out of Range\" error?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>A: You are either too far from the yard or your device's Location Services (GPS) are disabled</p>"},{"id":"schedule-pick-up-q-can-i-pick-up-multiple-cars-at-once","section":"Schedule Pick Up","question":"Q: Can I pick up multiple cars at once?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>A: Yes, if they are at the same yard, select multiple invoices before clicking \"Schedule Pickup.\"</p>"},{"id":"schedule-pick-up-q-how-do-i-visit-the-office-for-keys-or-payments","section":"Schedule Pick Up","question":"Q: How do I visit the office for keys or payments?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>A: Use the Visitor Sign-In option, enter your Lot # and DL #, and join the virtual queue</p><p>Top of Form</p>"},{"id":"third-party-lot-inspection-what-are-third-party-inspections","section":"Third party lot inspection","question":"What are Third-party Inspections?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Third-party vehicle inspections refer to the evaluation of a vehicle’s condition conducted by an independent inspector authorized by a Copart member. These inspections are performed on behalf of the member within Copart facilities and are limited to visual assessments, in accordance with yard safety, security, and operational guidelines, to support informed bidding decisions.1. Overview and Membership Requirements -</p><p>Copart encourages members to conduct personal or third-party inspections for informed bidding decisions</p><p>Only active Copart members may inspect vehicles or authorize third-party inspectors</p>"},{"id":"third-party-lot-inspection-1-what-are-the-requirements-to-have-a-third-party-ins","section":"Third party lot inspection","question":"1. What are the requirements to have a third-party inspection?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Do I need a Copart membership to inspect a vehicle?</p><p>Yes. Only active Copart Members are permitted to conduct inspections or authorize a third-party inspector to visit a yard on their behalf</p><p>Does Copart provide an official inspection service?</p><p>Copart no longer utilizes the \"Advantage\" inspection service. Members are encouraged to hire their own independent third-party inspectors or visit the yard personally</p><p>Can my inspector use a diagnostic code reader (OBD-II)?</p><p>No. The use of tools of any kind, including diagnostic code readers and scanners, is strictly prohibited within the yard</p>"},{"id":"third-party-lot-inspection-2-what-are-the-different-coordination-approvals-requi","section":"Third party lot inspection","question":"2. What are the different Coordination & Approvals required for a third-party inspection?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Do I need permission from the seller before an inspection?</p><p>Yes. Yard staff must obtain a \"Third-Party Inspection Service Order\" from the seller unless that seller has a \"Blanket Approval\" policy in place. It is highly recommended to contact the yard in advance to confirm these requirements</p><p>Should I notify the yard before my inspector arrives?</p><p>Absolutely. Coordination with the specific Copart yard prior to arrival is mandatory to review \"Operations Notes\" and ensure the vehicle is accessible in a designated Sale Row</p><p>What information does the yard need to process my request?</p>"},{"id":"third-party-lot-inspection-how-can-i-ensure-a-smooth-inspection-for-my-hired-pro","section":"Third party lot inspection","question":"How can I ensure a smooth inspection for my hired professional?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Confirm your membership is active</p><p>Provide the inspector with the correct Lot/VIN list</p><p>Call the yard ahead of time to verify seller approval (Manual vs. Blanket)</p><p>Ensure the inspector knows they cannot bring tools or code readers</p><p>Remind the inspector to bring a safety vest and wear closed-toe shoes</p>"},{"id":"title-status-overview","section":"Title Status","question":"Title Status","kind":"overview","html":"<p>A. Member Self-Service Tracking:</p><p>Step 1: Navigate to Title Status-</p><p>Members should:</p><p>Go to Payments Tab</p><p>Select Payments Due</p><p>Locate the Title Status column</p><p>Available in:</p><p>Unpaid Invoices</p><p>Payment History</p><p>Step 2: Understand Title Status-</p><p>Hover over the Tool Tip (i) icon</p><p>View definitions based on:</p><p>Title Delivery Preference:</p><p>Shipped (Delivery)</p><p>Step 3: Shipping Tracking-</p><p>Once a shipping label is generated:</p><p>Tracking number appears in Title Status column</p><p>Member can:</p><p>Click “Track” hyperlink</p><p>Redirect to shipping provider’s website</p><p>Step 4: Alternative Tracking Locations-</p><p>Members can also check title status in:</p><p>Payments History</p>"},{"id":"title-type-overview","section":"Title Type","question":"Title Type","kind":"overview","html":"<p>To provide clear guidance on member bidding eligibility by evaluating license types against state/provincial regulations and vehicle title statuses</p><p>Verification Tool: Always enter the Lot Number into the 'License bid eligibility' tool in the member's account as the first step</p><p>Lot Research: Check Portal &gt; Lot Management for \"International Title Restriction.\" Verify the Original Title State code (e.g., NS = Nova Scotia, NB = New Brunswick). If a Canadian code is present, Canadian dealer licensing is typically required</p><p>General Title Types:</p>"},{"id":"types-of-sale-what-is-sale-type","section":"Types of Sale","question":"What is Sale type?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>A Sale Type in a Copart auction defines the rules and conditions under which a vehicle is awarded to the highest bidder. It indicates whether the sale is final at the end of the auction or subject to seller approval or further negotiation after the auction concludes</p><p>To participate in bidding, members must:</p><p>Have an active paid membership (Basic or Premier)</p><p>Be eligible to bid on the specific lot</p><p>Have sufficient buying power or available bids</p>"},{"id":"types-of-sale-what-are-the-different-types-of-sale-status","section":"Types of Sale","question":"What are the different types of Sale Status?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Every vehicle listed on Copart is assigned a Sale Status, which determines how the final transaction is handled after the auction ends</p><p>The vehicle is awarded immediately to the highest bidder at the end of the auction</p><p>No minimum price or seller approval is required, and the sale is final</p><p>On Approval Sale:</p><p>The seller has until 7:45 PM PT on the next business day to accept, reject, or counter the highest bid</p><p>The seller may still accept the original bid if the buyer declines a counteroffer</p><p>Weekends are not included in the approval period</p><p>Minimum Bid / On Reserve Sale:</p>"},{"id":"types-of-sale-what-are-the-immediate-purchase-options-for-members-to-purchase-lo","section":"Types of Sale","question":"What are the immediate Purchase Options For members to purchase lots?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Certain vehicles offer immediate purchase options, allowing members to secure a vehicle without participating in a live auction</p><p>Buy It Now:</p><p>This option is available for select vehicles under Minimum Bid sale status</p><p>It allows members to purchase the vehicle instantly at a fixed price set by the seller before the auction</p><p>After selecting Buy It Now, the member must confirm the purchase and proceed to payment</p><p>Payment must be completed within 3 business days, and 2 business days of free storage are provided (including the purchase day)</p><p>A pre-bid fee is applicable for Buy It Now transactions</p><p>Make an Offer:</p>"},{"id":"types-of-sale-where-can-a-member-view-the-sale-status-type-of-the-lot","section":"Types of Sale","question":"Where can a member view the Sale Status Type of the lot?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Prior to lot going into auction, the Sale Type will be listed on the lot page via the bidding window</p><p>Once the lot is in auction, the Sale Type will be listed within the information displayed per lot</p>"},{"id":"types-of-sale-what-is-a-counter-bid","section":"Types of Sale","question":"What is a Counter Bid?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Counter bid is a bid that the seller makes to counter the high bidder’s offer. Counter bids are made directly following the sale of vehicles designated as On Approval or On Reserve. Members acknowledge and agree that regardless of any counter bids made by the Seller, Members’ high bids on these vehicles shall remain open to acceptance by the Seller until 7:45 p.m. PST the next business day after the sale day</p>"},{"id":"types-of-sale-what-do-we-do-if-member-says-they-were-alerted-that-they-won-but-t","section":"Types of Sale","question":"What do we do if member says they were alerted that they won, but they do not see the lot invoice in their Payments Due page, what happened?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Check the Sale Type, if it was “On Approval” or “Minimum Bid” it may be pending on approval from seller. If yes, the seller has until 7:45 p.m. PST one business day after the auction to approve or reject the sale.</p>"},{"id":"types-of-sale-what-if-a-member-is-awarded-a-lot-but-does-not-wish-to-complete-th","section":"Types of Sale","question":"What if a member is awarded a lot but does not wish to complete the sale?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Please educate the member on relisting – if the lot is not paid within the 8 calendar days including day of sale, it will auto relist. If they wish to relist sooner, they will inquire with yard location. The relist fee will be 10% of sale price or $600, whichever is highest</p>"},{"id":"types-of-sale-what-member-fees-will-apply-to-a-lot-awarded","section":"Types of Sale","question":"What Member fees will apply to a lot awarded?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>For each lot a member wins, they will be charged a buyer fee, gate fee, internet bid fee, title pickup/mailing fee and an environmental fee</p><p>· Buyer fee – based on title type and sale price of the vehicle</p><p>· Internet bid fee - based on title type and sale price of the vehicle</p><p>· Gate fee - $79 for clean title and $95 for non-clean title type vehicles</p><p>· Environmental fee - $0 for clean title and $15 for non-clean title type vehicles</p>"},{"id":"types-of-sale-if-a-lot-is-awarded-via-buy-it-now-or-kiosk-bid-feature-what-virtu","section":"Types of Sale","question":"If a lot is awarded via Buy It Now or Kiosk Bid feature, what virtual bid fee will apply?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Both Buy It Now and Kiosk Bids will be charged as a “pre-bid” for the virtual bid fee</p>"},{"id":"types-of-sale-where-can-member-view-a-list-of-lots-that-offer-buy-it-now","section":"Types of Sale","question":"Where can member view a list of lots that offer “Buy It Now”?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>By selecting Inventory &gt; Vehicle finder &gt; Buy It Now (under Featured items)</p>"},{"id":"types-of-sale-for-on-approval-on-reserve-sales-can-a-member-reject-the-sellers-c","section":"Types of Sale","question":"For On Approval/On Reserve sales, can a member reject the Sellers Counter bid?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Members can stay at their current bid or counter the sellers offer but they cannot reject the sellers counter. If the buyer does not accept the seller counter, the seller can still accept the original bid within the timeframe (7:45pm PST the following business day)</p>"},{"id":"unapplied-funds-process-overview","section":"Unapplied funds process","question":"Unapplied funds process","kind":"overview","html":"<p>The objective of this document is to define unapplied funds and its usage in the member journey</p><p>What Are Unapplied Funds?      Unapplied funds (also called available funds) are payments a member has already sent to Copart but haven’t yet been applied to a specific invoice</p><p>These funds may come from:</p><p>An overpayment</p><p>A wire transfer sent in advance towards any future invoices on member’s account</p><p>Important:-Unapplied funds can only be added via wire transfer.</p><p>They are considered a secure payment method</p><p>How can members add Unapplied Funds:-</p><p>Members needs to make a payment via wire transfer</p>"},{"id":"unapplied-funds-process-how-can-members-apply-unapplied-funds-to-an-open-invoice","section":"Unapplied funds process","question":"How can members apply unapplied Funds to an open invoice?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>When a member wants to use their available funds, please guide the member using the below steps -</p><p>Step 1: Guide member to select the invoice they would like to pay for using the below steps -</p><p>Go to Open Invoices</p><p>Check the box next to the invoice</p><p>Step 2: Guide member to choose payment type using the below steps -</p><p>On the Payment Information screen</p><p>Select Unapplied Funds</p><p>Click Add to Payment List</p><p>Step 3: Guide member to review &amp; confirm their payment using the below steps -</p><p>Check the Applied Payments List on the right</p><p>Click Confirm Payment</p><p>(If needed, use Reset Payment to start over)</p>"},{"id":"unapplied-funds-process-how-can-agents-apply-unapplied-funds-to-an-open-invoice","section":"Unapplied funds process","question":"How can Agents apply unapplied Funds to an open invoice?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Step 1: Open the member account on Member S&amp;M portal</p><p>Step 2: Go to Member payments tab</p><p>Step 3: Select the open invoice and click on pay (Do confirm the lot number with the member before selecting the invoice)</p><p>Step 4: Select unapplied funds while choosing the payment method</p><p>Step 5: Click Add to payment list</p><p>Step 6: Click on Confirm payment after confirming/getting authorization from the member to apply the available funds in their account towards the invoice</p><p>Split Payment Process (Using Unapplied Funds) :-</p><p>Because unapplied funds are a secure payment option, they can be combined with other secure payment methods</p>"},{"id":"unapplied-funds-process-how-are-refund-for-unapplied-funds-processed","section":"Unapplied funds process","question":"How are refund for Unapplied funds processed?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>For members registered within US/Canada address: Members will receive a check refund within 30 calendar days</p><p>For members with International address : Members will receive their funds via Wire transfer in 3-4 weeks</p><p>For membership renewal invoices, partial payments are not accepted when Unapplied Funds are insufficient to cover the full balance</p><ul><li>Can unapplied funds be combined with other payment methods?</li></ul><p>Yes. Since unapplied funds are secure, they can be combined with other secure funds only:</p><p>Western Union</p><p>Example:A member partially pays with a debit card and applies unapplied funds to cover the remaining balance</p>"},{"id":"vehicle-alerts-overview","section":"Vehicle Alerts","question":"Vehicle Alerts","kind":"overview","html":"<p>What is Vehicle Alert? A Vehicle Alert is a user-configured notification service that automatically informs users (via email, SMS, or mobile push notifications) when vehicles matching their specified search criteria (such as make, model, year, or other attributes) are added to inventory, eliminating the need for repeated manual searches</p><p>What is the process for Vehicle Alerts? Step 1- Initial Search-</p><p>The user performs a vehicle search via the Vehicle Finder or Inventory tab on the Copart platform (desktop, mobile, or app)</p><p>Step 2- Trigger for Alert Setup-</p>"},{"id":"vehicle-alerts-1-how-many-alerts-can-i-set-up","section":"Vehicle Alerts","question":"1- How many alerts can I set up?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>A: You can set up as many alerts as you want</p>"},{"id":"vehicle-alerts-2-can-i-change-how-often-i-receive-these-emails","section":"Vehicle Alerts","question":"2- Can I change how often I receive these emails?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>A: Yes, you can change the frequency or cancel alerts at any time through the \"Manage Alerts\" section</p>"},{"id":"vehicle-alerts-3-what-is-the-fastest-way-to-get-notified","section":"Vehicle Alerts","question":"3- What is the fastest way to get notified?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>A: The Copart Mobile App is the best resource for real-time push notifications for both auction status and vehicle matches</p>"},{"id":"vehicle-alerts-4-what-happens-if-i-can-t-find-a-vehicle-using-the-search-bar","section":"Vehicle Alerts","question":"4- What happens if I can't find a vehicle using the search bar?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>A: Copart will automatically take you to the Vehicle Alerts form to ensure you are notified the moment a matching vehicle becomes available</p>"},{"id":"vehicle-finder-overview","section":"Vehicle Finder","question":"Vehicle Finder","kind":"overview","html":"<p>The purpose of vehicle finder is to provide a standardized method for users to efficiently locate vehicles by applying defined filters such as make, model, year, damages and location</p><p>What is Vehicle Finder      The Vehicle Finder on Copart is a tool designed to help users quickly locate vehicles that meet their specific criteria within Copart’s auction inventory</p><p>It allows users to filter and search vehicles based on:</p><p>Make, model, and year</p><p>Damage type or condition</p><p>Auction type or lot number</p><p>Self-Help steps Using Copart Website:</p><p>Step 1 - Open your preferred browsing site</p><p>Step 2 - Go to www.copart.com</p>"},{"id":"vehicle-finder-can-a-non-member-access-the-vehicle-finder","section":"Vehicle Finder","question":"Can a non-member access the Vehicle Finder?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Yes. The Vehicle Finder is available to everyone. Even users without a Guest Account or Digital Membership can use the filters to easily browse and locate vehicles</p>"},{"id":"vehicle-finder-do-i-have-to-sign-in-to-access-the-vehicle-finder","section":"Vehicle Finder","question":"Do I have to Sign-in to access the Vehicle Finder?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>No. This feature is available to everyone accessing the Copart website or the app</p>"},{"id":"vehicle-finder-can-i-use-vehicle-finder-to-view-no-license-required-vehicles","section":"Vehicle Finder","question":"Can I use Vehicle Finder to view “No License Required” vehicles?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Yes. Select All Vehicles &gt; Featured Items &gt; No License Required in the filters</p>"},{"id":"vehicle-finder-how-can-i-add-a-lot-to-the-watchlist","section":"Vehicle Finder","question":"How can I add a lot to the watchlist?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>To add a vehicle to your watchlist, type the lot number in the search bar. Then, on the lot images, click the star icon to add the vehicle to your watchlist</p>"},{"id":"vehicle-finder-why-add-lot-to-watchlist","section":"Vehicle Finder","question":"Why add lot to watchlist?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>If you don’t want to miss an auction or need to keep track of multiple vehicles, the watchlist helps you stay organized. It works like a reminder so you don’t miss anything important</p>"},{"id":"vehicle-finder-why-are-there-no-search-results","section":"Vehicle Finder","question":"Why are there no search results?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>If you selected a specific make, model, or year and no results appear, it means we currently do not have vehicles matching that criteria</p>"},{"id":"watchlist-overview","section":"Watchlist","question":"Watchlist","kind":"overview","html":"<p>Watchlist –Overview :-</p><p>The Watchlist feature allows members to track vehicles of interest before they appear in a live auction. It captures key details such as sale date, lot number, and current bid, and enables members to receive notifications related to auction activity</p><p>The Watchlist is available for all vehicles on the Copart website and mobile app and can be accessed by all membership types, including Guest and Digital members. The process scope concludes when a vehicle (lot) is either removed from the auction or successfully sold</p>"},{"id":"watchlist-how-to-access-watchlist-and-how-does-it-work","section":"Watchlist","question":"How to access Watchlist and how does it work?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Members must log in to their Copart account to use the Watchlist feature</p><p>During a vehicle search, members can select the “Watch” option to add a lot to their Watchlist or can click on the lot number and select “Watchlist” from top right corner to have that lot added under their watchlist section</p><p>A maximum of 2,000 lots can be saved at a time</p><p>The Watchlist can be accessed via the Dashboard or clicking the “inventory” option and selecting “Watchlist”</p><p>Members can view Watchlists on the Copart website or mobile application</p>"},{"id":"watchlist-1-how-to-subscribe-unsubscribe-to-watchlist-email-notifications","section":"Watchlist","question":"1- How to subscribe/unsubscribe to Watchlist email notifications?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Member must subscribe/unsubscribe to Watchlist notifications in their Preference Center</p><p>Sign in &gt; Profile Icon &gt; Preference Center &gt; Email Communication &gt; here member can click ‘Subscribe’ to receive email communications for items they have on their watchlist</p>"},{"id":"watchlist-2-what-are-lane-alerts","section":"Watchlist","question":"2-What are Lane Alerts?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Lane Alerts will send a notification via Text, Browser, and Mobile App Notification when a vehicle is up for Auction. These lots will be from the member’s Watchlist and those that they have placed a pre-bid on</p>"},{"id":"watchlist-3-how-will-the-members-identify-their-lot-is-watched-in-the-live-aucti","section":"Watchlist","question":"3-How will the members identify their lot is ‘watched’ in the live auction?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>The lot information box in the live auction will be gold in color</p>"},{"id":"bidder-process-what-is-an-enterprise-bidder","section":"Bidder Process","question":"What is an Enterprise Bidder?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>An Enterprise bidder is an authorized individual that has been granted the permission to use the Master Account’s Licensing to  bid and buy vehicles. This may be an Employee, Buyer, or Agent of the Company/Business</p><p>A Bidder on a Master Account has their own unique login (Username and Password) but operates within the Master Account's credentials.</p><p>Bidder Access &amp; Controls-</p><p>Bid Limits &amp; Buying Power:Bidders do not maintain individual deposits. They operate under the Master Account’s Premier Bid Limits, which can be adjusted at the discretion of the Enterprise Account Owner</p>"},{"id":"bidder-process-what-are-the-requirements-to-have-a-bidder-account","section":"Bidder Process","question":"What are the requirements to have a Bidder account?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Account must be a Premier Business and meet the Add Bidder Guidelines, which is based on tenure and account activity (Should at least be 6 months old and have 10 consecutive purchases over the last 6 months with no relist)</p><p>The Bidder must be 18 years of age</p><p>The Bidders Membership has an Annual cost of $249.00. The initial $249 must be added to the Enterprise account once the Bidder is approved and prior to the Bidder being added</p><p>Bidder Setup Process-</p><p>Form Submission:</p><p>Premier Owner and Bidder complete the Add Bidder Form</p><p>Required details: Name, Date of Birth, Phone Number, Email Address</p><p>Document Submission:</p>"},{"id":"bidder-process-verification-what-information-can-be-shared-to-enterprise-bidder","section":"Bidder Process","question":"Verification & What information can be shared to Enterprise bidder?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Bidders can only receive information regarding their bidder account – If they are a cardholder on the master account, they can receive information regarding the master account as well</p><p>Bidders cannot request to make changes to their account – Changes to the bidder name (marriage, legal name changes), or changes to the bidder email address must go through the master and submitted via Add/Delete bidder form, both parties must sign it as if it were new</p>"},{"id":"bidder-process-1-who-can-add-additional-bidders","section":"Bidder Process","question":"1- Who can add additional bidders?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Only Premier Business accounts and existing Enterprise accounts.  Basic Members are restricted to a single user</p>"},{"id":"bidder-process-2-how-is-the-buying-power-of-the-bidder-managed","section":"Bidder Process","question":"2- How is the Buying Power of the Bidder managed?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>The Enterprise Master controls Bid Limits and Buying power. They can increase and decrease the bid limits on each bidder within their Manage Bidders menu option once logged into the Master account. The bid limits on a Bidder account cannot exceed the limits of the Enterprise account</p><p>For example, the Master account has a buying power of $100k, and they are requesting a bidder be moved to $200k</p>"},{"id":"bidder-process-3-if-my-bidder-makes-a-mistake-am-i-responsible","section":"Bidder Process","question":"3- If my bidder makes a mistake, am I responsible?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Yes. The Master Account holder is legally and financially responsible for all bids placed by any authorized bidder</p>"},{"id":"bidder-process-4-can-i-add-a-copart-employee-as-a-bidder","section":"Bidder Process","question":"4-Can I add a Copart employee as a bidder?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>No. Under the Global Auction Integrity Policy, Copart personnel and contractors are strictly prohibited from bidding on vehicles or being associated with any member account</p>"},{"id":"bidder-process-5-can-a-bidder-s-account-status-be-changed-by-the-master","section":"Bidder Process","question":"5-Can a Bidder’s account status be changed by the Master?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Yes. The Master can Inactivate and Activate the Bidder’s account status at any time. Unless the Inactivation was enforced by Copart</p><p>For example, Inactivated due to excessive relists</p><p>Suspensions cannot be enforced or reinstated by the Enterprise account</p>"},{"id":"bidder-process-6-how-does-a-password-reset-work","section":"Bidder Process","question":"6- How does a Password reset work?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Password resets can be completed by the Enterprise account within their Manage Bidders menu. They can reset the password to the Bidders email address or to the Master’s email address. Member Services can reset the password to the Bidder or Enterprise account via the Bidder Maintenance Tab in MSM</p>"},{"id":"bidder-process-7-how-does-an-enterprise-change-the-email-on-a-bidder-account","section":"Bidder Process","question":"7- How does an Enterprise change the email on a Bidder account?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>The Enterprise and Bidder must submit the Add Bidder form with the updated Email address. Both individuals must sign the form in order for the request to be considered</p>"},{"id":"bidder-process-8-how-do-i-delete-a-bidder","section":"Bidder Process","question":"8- How do I Delete a bidder?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>The Enterprise account must complete the top portion of the Add/ Delete bidder form and submit it via the Document uploader on the Enterprise account. Once processed, the Bidder will be moved to Suspended status. The bidder number will exist for the lifespan of the account and cannot be reused by a different user</p>"},{"id":"bidder-process-9-can-a-bidder-pay-for-their-own-lots-and-pickup-titles","section":"Bidder Process","question":"9- Can a bidder pay for their own lots and pickup titles?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>No, the payments must come from the Enterprise account. Titles are issued to the Enterprise account Business name and mailed or picked up by the Enterprise</p><p>10- The bidder was approved but hasn’t been added yet. What can be done?       ○ If buyer calls regarding their bidder not being added yet, look for note from Kiyonna Hardy stating bidder was approved and are now needing funds applied to the account</p>"},{"id":"shipping-overview","section":"Shipping","question":"Shipping","kind":"overview","html":"<p>Process Overview -</p><p>Lot Award &amp; Gate Pass Generation-</p><p>Upon lot award, a six-digit Gate Pass PIN is automatically generated and displayed on the Payments Due page in the member dashboard</p><p>Members must review the Pickup/Delivery Status to confirm delivery eligibility</p><p>Delivery Order Process-</p><p>If delivery is available, the “Order Delivery” option is displayed</p><p>A delivery estimate is shown upon selection</p><p>The system auto-populates the registered delivery address</p><p>Members may select “+ Add New Address” if needed</p><p>The selected address must allow safe vehicle unloading</p><p>After confirming details, the member completes payment</p>"},{"id":"shipping-what-are-the-different-types-of-delivery","section":"Shipping","question":"What are the different types of delivery?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Local Yard Delivery-</p><p>Standard timeline: Within 8 business days post-payment</p><p>May vary due to weather and transport availability</p><p>Driver contacts member 24 hours prior to delivery</p><p>Live tracking not available</p><p>Status tracking via: Bid Status &gt; Lots Won &gt; Lot Left Location</p><p>If delivery fails, member may arrange third-party transport</p><p>Copart Delivered (Long Haul – U.</p><p>S. Only)-</p><p>Available only within the United States (not Canada)</p><p>Estimated timeline: 5–7 business days after payment</p><p>Support details shared post-order confirmation</p><p>Contact support:</p><p>Phone: (972) 940-4000</p><p>Email: copartdelivered.support@copart.com</p>"},{"id":"shipping-1-when-can-a-member-order-delivery-for-lot","section":"Shipping","question":"1-When can a member order delivery for  lot?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Once the lot is awarded and the payment is completed member can order the delivery for the lot</p>"},{"id":"shipping-2-can-a-member-change-the-delivery-address-after-awarding-the-lot","section":"Shipping","question":"2-Can a member change the delivery address after awarding the lot?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Yes. The system automatically displays the address linked to the member’s account, but the member can select “+ Add New Address” to enter a different delivery location</p><p>3-Can a member change the delivery address after placing the order for the lot ?</p><p>As long as the lot is at the yard, member will have an option to change the delivery address, once the delivery is in transit, member will not be able to change the delivery address</p>"},{"id":"shipping-4-what-is-the-local-yard-delivery-and-what-is-the-time-for-the-delivery","section":"Shipping","question":"4-What is the local yard delivery and what is the time for the delivery?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Local Yard Delivery ( is typically completed within 8 business days after payment is    made. However, delivery timelines may vary depending on weather conditions and    transporter availability. The driver will contact the member 24 hours before delivery. Live tracking is not available once the vehicle leaves the yard. Local yard delivery is only for in state deliveries</p>"},{"id":"shipping-5-what-is-copart-delivered-and-how-long-does-it-take","section":"Shipping","question":"5-What is Copart Delivered and how long does it take?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Copart Delivered is a domestic shipping service available within the U.</p><p>S. (not available for Canada). The estimated delivery timeline is 5–7 business days after       order placement and payment confirmation. For updates or assistance, members can contact support at (972) 940-4000 or email</p><p>copartdelivered.support@copart.com. Copart delivered includes delivery outside the state where the lot is purchased</p><p>6-Can a member send his friend or relative to pick up the lot?</p>"},{"id":"finding-vehicles-overview","section":"Finding Vehicles","question":"Finding Vehicles","kind":"overview","html":"<p>This process helps Copart members and customer support teams understand how to search for, evaluate, and research vehicles listed for auction on Copart. It covers all the tools and steps involved in finding the right vehicle, understanding what icons and terms mean, and making an informed decision before bidding</p>"},{"id":"finding-vehicles-what-is-the-finding-vehicles-process","section":"Finding Vehicles","question":"What is the Finding Vehicles Process?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Finding Vehicles is the process members use to search, filter, research, track, and evaluate vehicles listed for auction on Copart before deciding whether to bid. Copart provides tools such as the search bar, Vehicle Finder, filters, Lot Details pages, Vehicle Icons, Watchlist, alerts, vehicle reports, and inspection options to help members review available inventory and make a more informed bidding decision</p><p>The process can include:</p><p>Searching by keyword, year, make, model, condition, VIN, lot number, or location</p><p>Applying filters such as vehicle type, damage type, title type, odometer, state, or location</p>"},{"id":"finding-vehicles-how-do-i-search-for-vehicles-on-copart","section":"Finding Vehicles","question":"How do I search for vehicles on Copart?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Use the search bar at the top of any page to enter year, make, model, condition, or location. You can also go to Inventory &gt; Vehicle Finder to use guided filters. Results can be narrowed by title type, damage type, year, and distance</p>"},{"id":"finding-vehicles-what-information-is-on-a-lot-details-page","section":"Finding Vehicles","question":"What information is on a Lot Details page?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>The Lot Details page includes 10 digital photos, VIN, title type, primary and secondary damage codes, odometer details, estimated retail value, body style, engine type, number of cylinders, keys availability, fuel type, drive type, seller, sale date and time, and location. It also shows any vehicle icons and special notes</p>"},{"id":"finding-vehicles-what-are-vehicle-icons","section":"Finding Vehicles","question":"What are vehicle icons?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Icons are visual labels that appear on search results and lot detail pages to highlight important information. Examples include Run &amp; Drive, Engine Start, Flood Reconditioned, Offsite, Hybrid, CrashedToys, Donated, Seller Certified, Copart GO, VIX, and Copart Wholesale. Each icon has a specific meaning</p>"},{"id":"finding-vehicles-what-does-run-drive-mean","section":"Finding Vehicles","question":"What does Run & Drive mean?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>At the time of inventory, the vehicle started under its own power (or with a jump box), was put into gear, and moved forward. This is not a guarantee that it will start or be roadworthy at the time of sale or pickup</p>"},{"id":"finding-vehicles-what-are-damage-codes","section":"Finding Vehicles","question":"What are damage codes?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Damage codes indicate known or reported damage to a vehicle. There are two codes per vehicle: Primary Damage and Secondary Damage. Both are equally important. Codes include FR (Front End), RR (Rear End), HL (Hail), WA (Water/Flood), BN (Burn), and many more. Copart recommends always inspecting a vehicle before bidding</p>"},{"id":"finding-vehicles-how-do-i-learn-more-about-a-vehicle-before-bidding","section":"Finding Vehicles","question":"How do I learn more about a vehicle before bidding?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>You can view the vehicle in person at the yard (Mon–Fri during business hours), order a Copart Vehicle Inspection Report, review any free condition reports (Wholesale or GO reports), or hire a third-party inspector. Third-party vehicle history reports are also available on the Copart website</p>"},{"id":"finding-vehicles-how-do-i-add-a-vehicle-to-my-watchlist","section":"Finding Vehicles","question":"How do I add a vehicle to my Watchlist?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Click the Watch button on a vehicle’s search results listing or on its Lot Details page. The Watchlist tracks the sale date, lot number, and current bid. You can also set up email or text alerts to be notified when the vehicle is about to go live</p>"},{"id":"finding-vehicles-what-are-vehicle-alerts","section":"Finding Vehicles","question":"What are Vehicle Alerts?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>If a vehicle matching your search is not currently available, you can set up a Vehicle Alert. Copart will notify you when a matching vehicle becomes available for auction. Alerts can be set from the Vehicle Alerts option in the top navigation menu</p>"},{"id":"finding-vehicles-what-is-the-difference-between-a-pre-bid-and-a-live-bid","section":"Finding Vehicles","question":"What is the difference between a Pre-Bid and a Live Bid?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>A Pre-Bid is placed before the virtual auction begins and wins if no higher bid is offered during the live sale. A Live Bid is placed in real time during the virtual auction. A Monster Bid allows you to jump the current bid to a specific amount in one step rather than bidding incrementally</p>"},{"id":"finding-vehicles-what-does-a-sale-type-like-on-approval-or-pure-sale-mean","section":"Finding Vehicles","question":"What does a sale type like On Approval or Pure Sale mean?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Pure Sale: No minimum bid; the highest bidder wins at close of auction. On Approval: The seller can accept or reject the highest bid within 1 business day after the sale. Minimum Bid: The seller has set a minimum price; if not met, the seller may accept the highest offer or re-run the vehicle in a future auction</p>"},{"id":"licensing-requirements-overview","section":"Licensing Requirements","question":"Licensing Requirements","kind":"overview","html":"<p>This process helps Copart members understand when a license is required to bid on or buy vehicles through Copart. Whether a license is needed can depend on the state where the vehicle is located, the vehicle type, the title type, and the member's eligibility. The goal is to give members and support teams a simple, standardized way to check licensing rules before placing a bid</p>"},{"id":"licensing-requirements-what-are-licensing-requirements","section":"Licensing Requirements","question":"What are Licensing Requirements?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Licensing requirements are the rules that decide whether a member can bid on or buy a specific vehicle. Some vehicles can be purchased by the general public, while others may require a business license, dealer license, dismantler license, broker assistance, or other state-specific documents</p><p>These requirements are not the same for every vehicle. They may change depending on:</p><p>The state where the vehicle is located</p><p>The vehicle's title type</p><p>The vehicle's condition</p><p>The sale type</p><p>The member's account and license status</p><p>Buyer Account Types and What They Require to Bid</p><p>1. Domestic Individual Buyers</p>"},{"id":"licensing-requirements-why-do-i-need-a-license-to-buy-certain-vehicles","section":"Licensing Requirements","question":"Why do I need a license to buy certain vehicles?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Some states have rules about who can buy certain types of vehicles, especially salvage, dealer-only, or restricted-title vehicles. Because of these state rules, a business or dealer license may be needed before a member can bid on or buy those vehicles</p>"},{"id":"licensing-requirements-how-do-i-know-if-i-need-a-license","section":"Licensing Requirements","question":"How do I know if I need a license?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Check the licensing requirement for the state where the vehicle is located, then review the vehicle and title details before bidding. Copart's Help with Licensing page lets you select a state and see what is required there</p>"},{"id":"licensing-requirements-can-i-buy-a-vehicle-if-i-do-not-have-the-required-license","section":"Licensing Requirements","question":"Can I buy a vehicle if I do not have the required license?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>You may not be able to buy it directly. However, you may be able to purchase it through a Copart-approved Broker, or you can search for vehicles marked “No License Required,” which are open to the general public</p>"},{"id":"licensing-requirements-what-is-a-broker","section":"Licensing Requirements","question":"What is a Broker?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>A Broker is a licensed third party that can bid on and buy vehicles on your behalf when you do not have the required license. The Broker places the bid, completes the purchase, and usually charges a service fee. Availability depends on the vehicle and the state</p>"},{"id":"licensing-requirements-are-licensing-rules-the-same-in-every-state","section":"Licensing Requirements","question":"Are licensing rules the same in every state?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>No. Licensing rules vary from state to state. A vehicle in one state may have different requirements than a similar vehicle in another state, so you must check the requirements for each vehicle's location</p>"},{"id":"licensing-requirements-can-copart-provide-me-with-a-license","section":"Licensing Requirements","question":"Can Copart provide me with a license?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>No. Copart does not issue business, dealer, or state licenses. Members must obtain any required license through the correct state authority, such as the Department of Motor Vehicles (DMV) or its equivalent</p>"},{"id":"licensing-requirements-what-should-i-do-before-bidding","section":"Licensing Requirements","question":"What should I do before bidding?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Before bidding, review the licensing requirements for the vehicle's state, confirm your eligibility, check that any required documents are on file, and make sure you understand all the purchase rules</p>"},{"id":"licensing-requirements-what-happens-if-i-bid-without-the-required-license","section":"Licensing Requirements","question":"What happens if I bid without the required license?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>If you do not meet the licensing requirements, you may not be able to complete the purchase even if you win the bid. This is why it is important to check the requirements before placing any bid.</p><p>Sources: https://www.copart.com/helpWithLicensing and https://www.copart.com/content/us/en/licensing/licensingoverview</p><p>International buyers: https://www.copart.com/content/us/en/landing-page/international-buyers</p>"},{"id":"member-fees-overview","section":"Member Fees","question":"Member Fees","kind":"overview","html":"<p>This process helps Copart members understand the fees that are applied when they purchase a vehicle through Copart. By knowing what fees to expect, members can calculate their total budget accurately before placing a bid and avoid unexpected charges after winning</p>"},{"id":"member-fees-what-are-member-fees","section":"Member Fees","question":"What are Member Fees?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Member fees are the charges applied to a member’s account when they purchase a vehicle or item through Copart. The winning bid amount is only the starting point, several fees may be added on top of it. Knowing what fees to expect helps members plan their total purchase budget before placing a bid</p><p>Fees may differ based on:</p><p>The final winning bid amount</p><p>The vehicle title type, such as clean title or non-clean title</p><p>The type of vehicle, including standard vehicles or heavy/specialty vehicles</p><p>The type of bid placed, such as pre-bid, live bid, Buy It Now, or other online bidding methods</p>"},{"id":"member-fees-what-is-a-buyer-fee","section":"Member Fees","question":"What is a buyer fee?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>A buyer fee is a charge added to every vehicle purchased at Copart on top of the winning bid amount. The fee is based on a tiered schedule and depends on the final bid price and the type of vehicle (standard or heavy)</p>"},{"id":"member-fees-what-is-a-virtual-bid-fee","section":"Member Fees","question":"What is a Virtual Bid Fee?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>A virtual bid fee is charged whenever a member places a bid online, whether through the Copart website, app, smartphone, tablet, or any terminal. Pre-bids placed before the live sale are charged at a slightly lower rate than bids placed during the live virtual sale</p>"},{"id":"member-fees-what-is-the-gate-fee-and-does-everyone-pay-it","section":"Member Fees","question":"What is the Gate Fee and does everyone pay it?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>The gate fee is $95 and is charged on all Copart purchases. It covers the cost of moving the vehicle from the storage area to the buyer loading area, plus administrative costs. Every buyer pays this fee, with no exceptions</p>"},{"id":"member-fees-when-do-i-have-to-pay-for-my-vehicle","section":"Member Fees","question":"When do I have to pay for my vehicle?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Full payment must be made within 3 business days of the sale, including the day of sale. If the vehicle is not paid in full within this window, a $50 late fee per vehicle will be charged to the account</p>"},{"id":"member-fees-when-does-storage-start-and-how-much-does-it-cost","section":"Member Fees","question":"When does storage start, and how much does it cost?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>Storage fees begin to accrue after the allowed free pickup window has passed. Rates vary by location, so members should check the specific yard’s Locations page on the Copart website for the daily storage rate</p>"},{"id":"member-fees-what-is-a-relist-fee","section":"Member Fees","question":"What is a Relist Fee?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>If a vehicle is not paid in full within 8 calendar days of the sale (including the sale day), Copart will relist the vehicle. A relist fee of 10% of the final sale price will be charged, with a minimum of $600. This is charged in addition to any late fees already applied</p>"},{"id":"member-fees-what-is-the-mailing-fee","section":"Member Fees","question":"What is the Mailing Fee?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>A mailing fee of $50 is applied per lot to cover the cost of sending vehicle-related documents to the member</p>"},{"id":"member-fees-are-fees-the-same-for-all-types-of-vehicles","section":"Member Fees","question":"Are fees the same for all types of vehicles?","kind":"faq","html":"<p>The buyer fee schedule differs between standard vehicles and heavy vehicles at higher bid ranges. At lower bid amounts the fees are the same, but at higher amounts (above $8,000) heavy vehicles are charged a percentage rate while standard vehicles remain on a flat-fee scale</p>"}];
